# File: scripts/__tests__/plugin-root-materialization.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/604-resolve-plugin-root-in-single-quoted-and-glob-shell-operands-and-in-glob-and-grep-paths/requirements.md
Feature: Resolve <plugin-root> in single-quoted and glob shell operands and in Glob and Grep paths

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Single-quoted operands resolve
    Given the plugin root "/Volumes/Fast Brick/plugins/nmg-sdlc"
    And the Bash command "<command>"
    When the hooks module rewrites the command
    Then the command is "<rewritten>"

    Examples:
      | command                                         | rewritten                                                    |
      | ls '<plugin-root>/workflows'                    | ls '/Volumes/Fast Brick/plugins/nmg-sdlc/workflows'          |
      | cat '${NMG_SDLC_PLUGIN_ROOT}/references/a.md'   | cat '/Volumes/Fast Brick/plugins/nmg-sdlc/references/a.md'   |

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Glob operands still expand
    Given the plugin root "/Volumes/Fast Brick/plugins/nmg-sdlc"
    And the Bash command "ls <plugin-root>/workflows/<glob>"
    When the hooks module rewrites the command
    Then the command is "ls \"/Volumes/Fast Brick/plugins/nmg-sdlc\"/workflows/<glob>"
    And the glob characters are outside every quoted segment

    Examples:
      | glob                              |
      | draft-issue/references/*.md       |
      | ?.md                              |
      | [ab]*.md                          |

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Glob and Grep paths resolve
    Given the plugin root "/Volumes/Fast Brick/plugins/nmg-sdlc"
    And a <tool> tool call whose path is "<plugin-root>/workflows"
    When the hooks module handles the call
    Then the tool receives the path "/Volumes/Fast Brick/plugins/nmg-sdlc/workflows"

    Examples:
      | tool |
      | Glob |
      | Grep |

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Existing rewrites are preserved
    Given the plugin root "/Volumes/Fast Brick/plugins/nmg-sdlc"
    When the double-quoted, bare controller, environment-variable and non-script Bash commands and a Read path with a placeholder are rewritten
    Then each result equals its result before this change
